spec.patch_directive:
PATCH FORMAT (MANDATORY — this is an ADDITIVE edit that adds ONLY new top-level functions and must NOT alter any existing symbol). Emit a single __JANUSMASK_PATCHES__ list with EXACTLY ONE entry of kind 'symbol' whose `name` is the EXISTING module constant 'AUTO_SUBMIT_THRESHOLD'. In `code`, reproduce that anchor line BYTE-FOR-BYTE exactly as it appears in the staged read-only target ({WORK_DIR}/inbox/targets/ngv2/debate_router.py) — it is the single line `AUTO_SUBMIT_THRESHOLD = 0.9` — and then append your THREE new top-level functions (calculate_shannon_entropy, calculate_kl_divergence, early_stop) after it. The harness inserts the new functions next to the anchor and preserves every other byte of the file. DO NOT reproduce or modify route_finding, DebateFinding, _coerce_score, _extract_confidence, or any other existing symbol — they must remain untouched (the oracle asserts route_finding still returns 'auto_submit'/'auto_reject'/'debate' correctly, including for a DebateFinding input). DO NOT anchor on a function. DO NOT emit whole-file. Example shape:
__JANUSMASK_PATCHES__ = [
  {'file': 'ngv2/debate_router.py', 'kind': 'symbol', 'name': 'AUTO_SUBMIT_THRESHOLD', 'code': r'''AUTO_SUBMIT_THRESHOLD = 0.9

def calculate_shannon_entropy(probs):
    ...

def calculate_kl_divergence(p, q):
    ...

def early_stop(history, h_thresh=0.1, kl_thresh=0.05):
    ...'''},
]

